ead the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-verasnap-verify-sdk-20261118" class="status"><h2>VeraSnap Verify SDK 0.1.0: open-source server-side checks for CPP capture proofs</h2><p>VeritasChain Co., Ltd. published a Python verifier and device-key enrollment checks for VeraSnap proofs under Apache-2.0, for insurers that receive claim photos. It is a first-party alpha release and has not been independently audited.</p><p>First-party alpha release by the operator of VSO; not independently audited, not a conformance test suite and not a certification. A proof shows when and on which device a capture was recorded; it does not show that the picture is true.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-18-verasnap-verify-sdk-0-1-0/">Read the release notice, checks and limits</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="verification-hardening-20261115" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-15">2026-11-15</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-15-verification-hardening-explorer-update/">VSO reports 23 verification, SDK and Explorer improvements</a></h3><p class="news-summary">Five areas cover configured-key validation, safer inputs and outputs, unresolved verdicts, evidence-review research and the public Explorer. Current main, fixed distributions and…</p><details class="archive-record" id="verification-hardening-20261115-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-verification-hardening-20261115" class="status"><h2>VSO reports 23 verification, SDK and Explorer improvements</h2><p>Five areas cover configured-key validation, safer inputs and outputs, unresolved verdicts, evidence-review research and the public Explorer. Current main, fixed distributions and first-party CI remain distinct.</p><p>Experimental extensions and proposed repairs remain unadopted; independent third-party reproduction has not been established. First-party CI, separate-language recomputation, saved-evidence rechecks and an independent fresh run are distinct. Merges and synthetic successes do not establish full conformance, production safety or certification.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-15-verification-hardening-explorer-update/">Read changes, revisions and limits</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="cursor-apify-epoch-20261114" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-14">2026-11-14</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-14-cursor-apify-epoch-source-review/">Cursor follow-up, Apify and Epoch AI: secrets, permissions and evaluation boundaries</a></h3><p class="news-summary">Reviewing three 13 November reports and updates, with Cursor identified as a follow-up. Official reports, participant accounts, press reporting and VSO analysis are separate.…</p><details class="archive-record" id="cursor-apify-epoch-20261114-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-cursor-apify-epoch-20261114" class="status"><h2>Cursor follow-up, Apify and Epoch AI: secrets, permissions and evaluation boundaries</h2><p>Reviewing three 13 November reports and updates, with Cursor identified as a follow-up. Official reports, participant accounts, press reporting and VSO analysis are separate. Extensions remain unadopted; independent reproduction is not established.</p><p>Experimental extensions remain unadopted; independent third-party reproduction is not established. First-party CI is distinct from independent fresh execution. This article demonstrates no VAP/VCP prevention capability, full conformance or certification.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-14-cursor-apify-epoch-source-review/">Read the source distinctions and VSO analysis</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="snowball-grok-20261114" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-14">2026-11-14</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-14-snowball-grok-source-review/">Snowball and Grok Build reports: AI actions, publication permissions and evidence limits</a></h3><p class="news-summary">A source review of Snowball and Grok Build separates the Cisco correction, researcher estimates and VSO analysis. Extensions remain unadopted; independent reproduction is not…</p><details class="archive-record" id="snowball-grok-20261114-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-snowball-grok-20261114" class="status"><h2>Snowball and Grok Build reports: AI actions, publication permissions and evidence limits</h2><p>A source review of Snowball and Grok Build separates the Cisco correction, researcher estimates and VSO analysis. Extensions remain unadopted; independent reproduction is not established.</p><p>Experimental extensions remain unadopted; independent third-party reproduction has not been established. First-party CI success is distinct from independent fresh execution. This article establishes no VAP/VCP prevention record, full conformance or certification for these cases.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-14-snowball-grok-source-review/">Read corrections, estimates and VSO analysis</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="registry-release-20261113" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-13">2026-11-13</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-13-registry-release-known-issue/">VSO adds ten source reviews and a fixed-demo known-issue notice</a></h3><p class="news-summary">Ten source reviews added; the fixed demo now has a known-issue notice. Signature fix: main only, absent from fixed ZIP. Extensions unadopted; independent reproduction not…</p><details class="archive-record" id="registry-release-20261113-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-registry-release-20261113" class="status"><h2>VSO adds ten source reviews and a fixed-demo known-issue notice</h2><p>Website PR #224 adds ten reviews, bringing the registry to 64 entries: 19 registered and 45 source-verified, pending registration. The ten additions belong to the latter category. They are not ten newly confirmed incidents, and the total does not mean 64 registered cases.</p><p>PR #68 merged the explicit input policy into main. It is absent from the fixed tag, fixed ZIP and original 32-test record. This update changes the public explanation only: the tag, all five assets, checksums and historical execution evidence are retained. No replacement ZIP or new release is announced. Reports must pin the implementation commit.</p><p>Experimental extensions remain unadopted; independent third-party reproduction has not been established. Source checks, synthetic observations and CI described here are first-party work. Merging or passing CI does not establish full normative conformance, adoption, certification or production suitability.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-13-registry-release-known-issue/">Read updates, pinned revisions and limits</a> · <a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vap-spec/releases/tag/vap-interop-demo-v0.2.0">GitHub release</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="signature-source-20261112" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-12">2026-11-12</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-12-vap-signature-source-update/">VSO updates VAP references and research status; signature fix is on main only</a></h3><p class="news-summary">13 Nov: site CI at 720852c passed 110 image comparisons. Signature fix: main only, absent from fixed ZIP. Extensions unadopted; independent reproduction not established.</p><details class="archive-record" id="signature-source-20261112-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-signature-source-20261112" class="status"><h2>VSO updates VAP references and research status; signature fix is on main only</h2><p>VAP PR #68 strengthens Ed25519 input rejection in the experimental Python/Node interop demo. The fix is merged into main (35e56ba; included in e00ee5a). It is NOT included in the fixed vap-interop-demo-v0.2.0 ZIP, which remains at cbd4502. No replacement ZIP or new release is announced. Experimental extensions remain unadopted; independent third-party reproduction has not been established.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-12-vap-signature-source-update/">Read source revisions, the main/ZIP distinction and limitations</a></p><div id="original-main-ci-20261113"><h3>13 November follow-up: 110 image comparisons passed in site main CI</h3><p>Website vcp-site fix merge <code>720852c</code> completed all six workflows and 13 jobs. All 110 image comparisons passed with zero failures and zero raster-noise allowances. Incorrect-CSS rejection and animation checks also passed; comparison criteria were not relaxed. These are first-party CI results for this fixed website revision.</p><p>Experimental extensions remain unadopted; independent third-party reproduction is not established. This is not a new research-implementation test or independent reproduction. Earlier failures, historical test records and the distinction between fixed distributions and main are retained.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-12-vap-signature-source-update/#main-ci-20261113">Read the first-party CI revision, results and limits</a> · <a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vcp-site/actions/runs/43330507404">CI · 720852c</a></p></div></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="cloud-evidence-20261108" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-08">2026-11-08</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-08-cloud-evidence-maintenance-update/">VSO reports ten merged cloud-evidence and maintenance updates</a></h3><p class="news-summary">Ten merged PRs cover cloud-evidence research, interop release preparation and maintenance. The demo was unpublished at the initial review; a later experimental prerelease is…</p><details class="archive-record" id="cloud-evidence-20261108-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-cloud-evidence-20261108" class="status"><h2>VSO reports ten merged cloud-evidence and maintenance updates</h2><p>Ten merged PRs cover cloud-evidence research, interop release preparation, Explorer dependency maintenance, local-settings guards and incident-source records. PR #61 is release preparation and was unpublished at the initial review. A later experimental prerelease at 12:09 JST on 8 November is recorded separately in the linked article. The research is unadopted; independent reproduction is not established. Test and CI records are first-party checks, not independent confirmation.</p><p>All cloud experiments are synthetic and operated by the same party; no live cloud calls were made. They do not prove Azure origin, complete observation, independent custody, latestness, third-party timestamps, power-loss durability or production readiness. A valid older snapshot can remain valid without a separately retained contradictory checkpoint. Verification of custody does not grant permission to publish evidence. First-party CI is not independent reproduction.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-08-cloud-evidence-maintenance-update/">Read the ten updates, CI and limitations</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="payment-research-20261107" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-07">2026-11-07</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-07-payment-evidence-research-update/">VSO publishes seven VAP payment-evidence research and AI design updates</a></h3><p class="news-summary">VAP #52–#58 cover payment evidence, dispatch recovery, two-person approval and collection, plus school-AI and consumer-agent design notes. First-party CI only; unadopted,…</p><details class="archive-record" id="payment-research-20261107-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-payment-research-20261107" class="status"><h2>VSO publishes seven VAP payment-evidence research and AI design updates</h2><p>VAP #52–#58 were merged on 6 November. First-party payment-research CI checked 57 offline-evidence, 28 dispatch/recovery, 20 authorization and 25 collector tests separately. School-AI and consumer-agent updates are documents; the latter’s eight review cases are unexecuted. Extensions and proposals remain unadopted; independent reproduction is not established.</p><p>All experiments use first-party synthetic environments. A holder of raw mock-provider credentials can bypass the wrapper. Complete route coverage, independent custody, external anchoring, OS privilege separation and full proposal conformance are not established. A signed ACK does not prove truth, completeness or continuing retention.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-07-payment-evidence-research-update/">Read the seven updates, CI and limitations</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="research-sdk-20261105" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-05">2026-11-05</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-05-vap-research-sdk-reproduction/">VAP research, SDK updates and external reproduction notes</a></h3><p class="news-summary">5 Nov: a18cda8 site CI completed (110 image comparisons; 55 regression tests). Research remains unadopted; independent reproduction is not established.</p><details class="archive-record" id="research-sdk-20261105-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-research-sdk-20261105" class="status"><h2>VAP research, SDK updates and external reproduction notes</h2><p>Merged research separates control observations, wallet authorization and execution evidence. SDK fixes and reproduction notes are available; independent reproduction is not established.</p><p>Experimental extensions remain unadopted; independent third-party reproduction has not been established. The results below are first-party CI and internal research checks, not an independent assessment, certification, production-readiness determination or proof of complete observation.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-05-vap-research-sdk-reproduction/">Read the update and source records</a></p><div id="original-main-ci-20261105"><h3>5 November follow-up: site main CI completed</h3><p>Website main <code>a18cda8</code> completed all five workflows and 12 jobs, including 110 image comparisons, 55 regression tests and a 428-page CSP crawl. Chinese VeraSnap image pairs matched exactly at desktop and mobile widths. Comparison criteria were not relaxed.</p><p>This is first-party website CI, not an independent reproduction result. Experimental extensions remain unadopted; independent reproduction is not established. Historical test records remain attached to their original revisions.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-05-vap-research-sdk-reproduction/#main-ci-20261105">Read the main CI completion results and scope</a></p></div></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="github-corrections-20261103" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-03">2026-11-03</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-03-verification-status-explorer-corrections/">VSO updates verification-status disclosures and the public Explorer</a></h3><p class="news-summary">VAP source/hash, public Explorer and 23 merged corrections. First-party checks are distinct from independent reproduction; experimental extensions remain unadopted.</p><details class="archive-record" id="github-corrections-20261103-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-github-corrections-20261103" class="status"><h2>VSO updates verification-status disclosures and the public Explorer</h2><p>23 merged repository corrections: current VAP text and digest, bounded Explorer hash-chain checks, authentication fixes and historical-status disclosures. Experimental extensions remain unadopted; independent reproduction is not established.</p><p>These are disclosure corrections, bounded implementation repairs and first-party checks. They do not establish full VCP/VAP conformance, certification, production readiness or independent third-party reproduction. Experimental extensions remain <strong>unadopted</strong>; independent reproduction is <strong>not established</strong>. A local test reported in a PR, first-party CI, this website deployment check and an independent new execution are different records.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-03-verification-status-explorer-corrections/">Read the corrections and their limits →</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="github-update-20261102" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-02">2026-11-02</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-02-service-permission-receiver-state/">2 November: five service-permission and receiver-history research updates</a></h3><p class="news-summary">Evidect #30–#34 add synthetic permission and receiver-state experiments. Latest first-party CI passed 306 tests per Ubuntu/macOS job. Extensions remain unadopted; independent…</p><details class="archive-record" id="github-update-20261102-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-github-update-20261102" class="status" style="scroll-margin-top:10rem"><h2 style="margin-top:0">2 November: five service-permission and receiver-history research updates</h2><p>Evidect #30–#34 add service-permission rechecks, saved ten-case verification, checkpoint expiry/generations/key revocation and challenge-bound checks against a separate store. Latest merged eeeacf7 passed 306 tests per Ubuntu/macOS first-party CI job (44 new + 262 existing).</p><p>These are same-controller synthetic experiments. Separate processes and keys do not establish independent administration; both-store rollback and other limits remain. Extensions are <strong>unadopted</strong>; independent third-party reproduction is <strong>not established</strong>. The 137-test record, earlier results and fixed distributions are preserved.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-02-service-permission-receiver-state/">Read the five updates and their limits →</a></p></section>
